ING ORDER—VEXATIOUS LITIGANT\n\nCode of Civil Procedure, § 391.7  \nwww.courts.ca.gov--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVL-100\n | FOR COURT USE ONLY\n--- | ---\nCASE NAME: (https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/vl100.pdf)\nciteturn1653search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; VL-100 ... courts of California without approval of the presiding justice or presiding judge of the court in which the action is to be filed. ... www.courts.ca.gov\nVL-100\n | FOR COURT USE ONLY\n--- | ---\nCASE NAME:  | \nPREFILING ORDER—VEXATIOUS LITIGANT  | CASE NUMBER:Name and address of each plaintiff or cross-complainant or other party subject to this prefiling order:\n1. \nthe court\nparty\nThis prefiling order is entered pursuant to a motion made by\n(name):\n2.  \n3. \nThe person or persons identified in item 1, unless represented by an attorney, are prohibited from filing any new litigation in the \ncourts of California without approval of the presiding justice or presiding judge of the court in which the action is to be filed.\n4. \nThe clerk is ordered to provide a copy of this order to the Judicial Council of California by fax at 415-865-4329 or by mail \nat the address below.\nVexatious Litigant Prefiling Orders \nJudicial Council of California \n455 Golden Gate Avenue \nSan Francisco, California 94102-3688\nDate:\nJUDICIAL OFFICER\nPage 1 of 1\nForm Adopted for Mandatory Use \nJudicial Council of California \nVL-100 [Rev. September 1, 2018]\nPREFILING ORDER—VEXATIOUS LITIGANT\nCode of Civil Procedure, § 391.7 \nwww.courts.ca.gov\nPrint this form\nSave this form\nClear this form\nFor your protection and privacy, please press the Clear \nThis Form button after you have printed the form.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrefiling Order—Vexatious Litigant | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/VL-100)\nciteturn1653search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # Prefiling Order—Vexatious Litigant (VL-100)States the court’s decision (order) that a person cannot file a new case in a California court without first getting permission of the leader of the court.\n\n# Prefiling Order—Vexatious Litigant (VL-100)\n\nStates the court’s decision (order) that a person cannot file a new case in a California court without first getting permission of the leader of the court.\n\nGet form VL-100\n\nEffective: September 1, 2018--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPPENDIX A (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files?file=file%2Fappendix.pdf)\nciteturn1653search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; <tr><td>VL-100*</td><td>9/1/2018</td><td>Prefiling Order—Vexatious Litigant</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>VL-110</td><td>9/1/2018</td><td>Request and Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant</td><td></td></tr>\nJUDICIAL COUNCIL FORMS\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr><th>Form number</th><th>Effective date</th><th>Form title</th><th>[Rev. July 1, 2025]</th></tr>\n<tr><td>UD-125*</td><td>10/1/2021</td><td>Application to Prevent Forfeiture Due to COVID-19 Rental Debt</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>UD-150*</td><td>1/1/2005</td><td>Request/Counter-Request to Set Case for Trial—Unlawful Detainer</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>UD-155</td><td>1/1/2024</td><td>Eviction Case (Unlawful Detainer) Stipulation</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><th colspan=\"4\">Vexatious Litigants</th></tr>\n<tr><td>VL-100*</td><td>9/1/2018</td><td>Prefiling Order—Vexatious Litigant</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>VL-110</td><td>9/1/2018</td><td>Request and Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>VL-115</td><td>9/1/2018</td><td>Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>VL-120</td><td>9/1/2018</td><td>Application for Order to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner From Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List</td><td></td></tr>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVexatious Litigant List | Judicial Branch of California (https://courts.ca.gov/news-reference/reports-publications/vexatious-litigant-list)\nciteturn1653search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; VL-100, Prefiling Order—Vexatious Litigant. ... This optional form may be used by an individual that has been determined to be a vexatious litigant and who must obtain prior court approval to file any new litigation in which the vexatious litigant is not represented by an attorney. ... If you have any questions about this list, please contact VexatiousLitigantGroup@jud.ca.gov.\n\n## Other Requirements and Considerations\n\nThe Judicial Council’s annual dissemination of the vexatious litigant list to court clerks is required. To remove a name from the vexatious litigant list, the council must receive an order directly from the issuing court vacating the prefiling order.\n\nPlease note that if a person has been declared a vexatious litigant, but there is no prefiling order, or if there is an order requiring posting of security but no prefiling order, the name will not appear on the list.\n\n## Forms\n\nVL-100, Prefiling Order—Vexatious Litigant.\nThis mandatory Judicial Council form is to be used by the courts or a party when declaring a person or organization a vexatious litigant requiring a prefiling order.\n\nVL-110, Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant\nThis optional form may be used by an individual that has been determined to be a vexatious litigant and who must obtain prior court approval to file any new litigation in which the vexatious litigant is not represented by an attorney. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPPENDIX A (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files?file=rules-court%2Fappendix.pdf)\nciteturn1653search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; | UD-116 | 7/1/2003 | Declaration for Defau